  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1039 PM CST SAT NOV 7 2026\n\nWe are cooling off nicely this evening with temperatures already\ndown into the upper 40s to mid 50s. Lows in the mid 30s, light\nwinds, and narrowing dew point depressions will promote patchy\nfrost across the region late tonight through roughly 7 AM Sunday\nmorning. Similar conditions are expected Sunday night into Monday\nmorning so we will likely see another Frost Advisory issued as we\nwrap up the weekend.\n\nDry air and surface high pressure will keep us dry as we head\nthrough the first half of the work week. The upper level pattern\nstarts to pick up a bit by mid week with a southern stream trough\nlifting across the Southern Plains. Enough moisture looks to pool\nacross the region ahead of this feature to warrant a low chance\nof rain late Wednesday through Thursday afternoon. A stronger\nupper level trough quickly rips across much of the eastern US\nThursday through the weekend. An associated cold front will be\nsent our way on Thursday with a reinforcing surge of high\npressure arriving over the weekend. Limited moisture will lead to\na dry FROPA with this late week system.\n\nTemperatures will slowly warm through the work week with highs\nrebounding into the low to mid 70s by Tuesday/Wednesday.\nThursday's cold front will bring another shot of cooler air to\nthe region with highs struggling to break out of the 50s. Lows\nwill plummet into the low to mid 30s next week. Latest NBM\nprobabilities hint at 50-70% chance of seeing freezing temps\nacross our northern counties Saturday and Sunday mornings.\n\n95/Castillo",
